UnitTokenNFT::constructor
├── when the leaf voter is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the token registry is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
└── when the parameters are valid
    ├── it should set the name
    ├── it should set the symbol
    ├── it should set the LEAF VOTER immutable
    └── it should set the TOKEN REGISTRY immutable

UnitTokenNFT::mint
├── when the caller is not the registry
│   └── it should revert with NotRegistry
└── given the caller is the registry
    ├── when there are no records
    │   ├── it should mint the id to the recipient
    │   └── it should not emit RecordChanged
    ├── when there are records
    │   ├── it should mint the id to the recipient
    │   ├── it should write each record value
    │   └── it should emit RecordChanged with _id, _indexedKey, _key, _value for each record
    └── when the recipient is a receiver contract
        ├── it should mint the id to the recipient
        └── it should write the records before invoking the receiver

UnitTokenNFT::setRecord
├── when the id does not exist
│   └── it should revert with ERC721NonexistentToken
└── given the id exists
    ├── when the caller is not authorized
    │   └── it should revert with NotAuthorized
    ├── given the caller is the owner
    │   ├── when the key is unset
    │   │   ├── it should write the record value
    │   │   └── it should emit RecordChanged with _id, _indexedKey, _key, _value
    │   └── when the key already holds a value
    │       ├── it should overwrite the previous value
    │       └── it should emit RecordChanged with _id, _indexedKey, _key, _value
    ├── when the caller is approved for the token
    │   ├── it should write the record value
    │   └── it should emit RecordChanged with _id, _indexedKey, _key, _value
    └── when the caller is approved for all
        ├── it should write the record value
        └── it should emit RecordChanged with _id, _indexedKey, _key, _value

UnitTokenNFT::setRecords
├── when the id does not exist
│   └── it should revert with ERC721NonexistentToken
└── given the id exists
    ├── when the caller is not authorized
    │   └── it should revert with NotAuthorized
    ├── given the caller is the owner
    │   ├── when there are records
    │   │   ├── it should write each record value
    │   │   └── it should emit RecordChanged with _id, _indexedKey, _key, _value for each record
    │   ├── when there are no records
    │   │   └── it should not emit RecordChanged
    │   └── when the batch contains duplicate keys
    │       └── it should store the last value for the duplicated key
    ├── when the caller is approved for the token
    │   └── it should write each record value
    └── when the caller is approved for all
        └── it should write each record value

UnitTokenNFT::seize
├── when the caller is not a seizer
│   └── it should revert with NotSeizer
└── given the caller is a seizer
    ├── when the id does not exist
    │   └── it should revert with ERC721NonexistentToken
    └── given the id exists
        ├── when the recipient is the zero address
        │   └── it should revert with ERC721InvalidReceiver
        └── given the recipient is not the zero address
            ├── when the recipient is a new owner
            │   ├── it should transfer the nft to the new owner
            │   ├── it should preserve the records
            │   └── it should emit Seized with _id, _to
            ├── when the previous owner sets a record after a seize
            │   └── it should revert with NotAuthorized
            └── when an address the previous owner approved sets a record after a seize
                └── it should revert with NotAuthorized

UnitTokenNFT::transferFrom
├── when transferring to a new owner
│   ├── it should move ownership to the new owner
│   └── it should preserve the records
├── when the new owner sets a record after a transfer
│   ├── it should write the record value
│   └── it should emit RecordChanged with _id, _indexedKey, _key, _value
└── when the previous owner sets a record after a transfer
    └── it should revert with NotAuthorized

UnitTokenNFT::safeTransferFrom
├── when the recipient does not implement the receiver interface
│   └── it should revert with ERC721InvalidReceiver
└── when transferring to a new owner
    └── it should move ownership to the new owner

UnitTokenNFT::records
├── when there are no keys
│   └── it should return an empty array
└── when called
    ├── it should return the stored value for a set key
    └── it should return an empty value for an unset key
